<title>AUSTRALIA: EEC's Singa could hold 500 bcf, analysts.</title>
<headline>EEC's Singa could hold 500 bcf, analysts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production tests at the Singa-1 well in South Sumatra were in line with gas reserve estimates of about 500 billion cubic feet (bcf), analysts said on Monday.</p>
<p>Operator Energy Equity Corp Ltd earlier reported production testing at the exploration well had confirmed a new field gas discovery, with a flow of 20.3 million cubic feet per day over 12-1/4 hours through a 40/64 inch choke.</p>
<p>The test was carried out over the lower third, or poorest reservoir quality, of the Batu Raja formation and was in line with expectations, EEC said.</p>
</text>
